## Plugin Architecture

- Minimal contract: `name`, `version`, `init(ctx)`, `destroy()`; optional hooks (`onAppReady`, `onWindowCreated`)
- Validate the plugin shape before loading; load with `import()` from a configured directory or manifest
- Give plugins a narrow `ctx` API, not app internals; run untrusted plugins in a `utilityProcess`
- Isolate hook errors — one plugin must not crash the app; support unload via `destroy()`

---

## Performance Monitoring

- Sample `app.getAppMetrics()` and `process.memoryUsage()` every 5–10s; keep a bounded ring buffer
- Track window count, IPC call count, and IPC latency per channel
- Flag monotonic heap growth across sessions as a leak signal; never include PII in metrics

---

## Error Handling and Recovery

- `render-process-gone`: log reason/exit code, then reload or recreate the window, or show a recovery screen
- `child-process-gone` / `utilityProcess` `exit`: restart with bounded backoff
- Non-critical feature failure → disable the feature and continue
- When recovery fails, show a clear message with restart/report options; send crash reports (`crashReporter`) with consent

---

## Anti-Patterns

- Windows created ad hoc from multiple modules
- IPC channel strings duplicated across main, preload, and renderer
- Unbounded metric or error history
- Plugins with direct access to the window manager or file system
- Swallowing errors in recovery paths

---

## Checklist

- [ ] Central window manager; state persisted and restored within display bounds
- [ ] IPC contract shared and typed; structured errors; long operations report progress
- [ ] Plugins validated, isolated, and unloadable
- [ ] Bounded metrics; leak trend monitored
- [ ] Renderer and child process crashes handled with recovery or user feedback
